  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "xmlParseNCNameComplex",
    "file": "libxml2/parser.c",
    "description": "xmlParseNCNameComplex computes a token length (`len`) by advancing with CUR_CHAR/NEXTL over a UTF-8/encoding-dependent stream, then passes `(BASE_PTR + startPosition, len)` directly to xmlDictLookup. In this PoV, malformed multi-byte/encoding data causes `len` to exceed the actual contiguous bytes available from that start pointer (near static classification tables), so xmlDictLookup/xmlDictAddString performs memcpy(name, len) and over-reads into the global redzone (`xmlIsPubidChar_tab`). The root bug is missing bounds validation that `start+len` stays within the current input buffer before dictionary lookup/copy.",
    "conditions": "Triggered through the xslt harness when parsing an imported stylesheet (`xsl:import href=\"article.xsl\"`) loaded by xsltDocDefaultLoaderFunc. The imported document contains malformed encoding/name bytes (non-ASCII high bytes and broken markup) so the NCName scanner in xmlParseNCNameComplex derives an unsafe length from parser state. When that name is interned via xmlDictLookup -> xmlDictAddString, memcpy reads `len` bytes from an invalid source range, causing global-buffer-overflow. Requires crafted stylesheet content that reaches NCName parsing in libxml2 with inconsistent character-length vs available-byte boundaries."
  },
